.\" Man page for portscope.
.TH PORTSCOPE 1 "2026-10-22" "portscope 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
portscope \- inspect local ports, processes, systemd services and journal logs
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B portscope
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B PortScope
shows which local TCP and UDP endpoints are listening, which process owns each
one, which systemd unit that process belongs to, and what the journal says
about it.
.PP
Every endpoint\(hyservice link carries the evidence that produced it: a socket
inode seen in the process file descriptor table, a cgroup match, a
.B MainPID
match, socket activation via
.BR Triggers= ,
or a
.B Listen=
match. PortScope never infers an association from a port number, a process
name or a unit description. When there is no evidence it reports that no
association could be confirmed.
.PP
The application runs entirely as the invoking user. It does not request root,
does not use
.BR sudo ,
.BR pkexec
or polkit, does not modify group membership, and performs no network access.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-help
Show a summary of options.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Show the version.
.SH PERMISSIONS
Endpoint data, the socket owner UID and the socket cgroup are available to any
user, because
.B ss \-e
exposes them. For endpoints owned by other users the owning process is usually
recovered through
.BR /sys/fs/cgroup/<unit>/cgroup\.procs ,
which is world readable.
.PP
The system journal is readable only if the user is a member of
.B adm
or
.B systemd\-journal.
PortScope reports this as a permission limitation and continues to show the
remaining diagnostics; it does not present an unreadable journal as an empty
one, and it will not add you to any group.
.PP
Reading
.B /proc/<pid>/cmdline
of other users requires that
.B hidepid
is not set to 2. When it is, the command line is reported as unavailable.
.SH KEYBOARD
.TP
.B Ctrl+F
Focus the search field.
.TP
.B Ctrl+R
Collect the current state immediately.
.TP
.B Esc
Leave the details page in the narrow layout.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/portscope/settings.ini
User preferences (language). No collected data is ever written to disk.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR portscope-cli (1),
.BR ss (8),
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR journalctl (1)
.SH BUGS
No public bug tracker exists yet.
